232	    /**
233	     * Normalizes a postal address into a canonical form: surrounding whitespace is trimmed and
234	     * internal runs of whitespace collapsed to a single space, the value is upper-cased and common
235	     * abbreviations are expanded as whole tokens ({@code ST -> STREET}, {@code RD -> ROAD},
236	     * {@code AVE -> AVENUE}). So {@code '  12  main  st '} is stored and returned as
237	     * {@code '12 MAIN STREET'}.
